 infectious disease expert does say  in hindsight mandates were coercive and  says lockdowns and how people were  affected should be examined for next  time there has been a significant  erosion of trust that's happened while  protesters have called for freedom  others say vaccines restored the freedom  to go out and feel safer doing so that  freedom of choice on vaccines ignores  the risks there's no such thing as total  freedom even people who choose to get  unvacciated we society pays for their  hospital bills we generally live in a  society where we have to make  concessions for the greater good  the protests have revealed deep rifts in  the country and even the police  crackdown is triggering a necessary  debate but the larger story of the  pandemic is two years of collective  perseverance by canadians that is  gradually seeing health restrictions  finally lifted which is what everyone  wants  eric sorensen global news toronto  and that is global national for this  friday i'm jeff semple we leave you  tonight with one final look at the  situation in ottawa this overlooking  parliament hill we'll continue to follow  this developing story throughout tonight  and this weekend hope to see you back  here again tomorrow thanks for watching  have a great night
 

